      "url": "https://www.yorkshire-aircraft.co.uk/aircraft/yorkshire/york43/bb373.html",
      "title": "Halifax BB373 and JB874 collision, Hull Bridge (BB373 page)",
      "publisher": "yorkshire-aircraft.co.uk",
      "tier": "researched",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-28",
      "summary": "Regional crash researcher's account of the collision, with a full table of the eight BB373 crew: rank, service number, age, home town and burial. The page title misprints the serial as BB393.",
      "key_details": [
        "BB373 crew all killed",
        "collision 04:30 over Hull Bridge",
        "78 Squadron lost five aircraft and 31 airmen that night"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S2",
      "url": "https://www.yorkshire-aircraft.co.uk/aircraft/yorkshire/york43/jb874.html",
      "title": "Halifax JB874, Hull Bridge, Tickton",
      "publisher": "yorkshire-aircraft.co.uk (JB874 page)",
      "tier": "researched",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-28",
      "summary": "Same researcher's page for JB874, with the seven-man crew table. Six died; Sgt J. Greet was seriously injured and spent about five years recovering. Does not name the BB373 crew.",
      "key_details": [
        "Greet only survivor, no first name",
        "two of the dead may have died of injuries"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S3",
      "url": "https://www.cwgc.org/stories/stories/pilot-officer-edward-platt-137558-navigator-78-squadron-raf-bomber-command/",
      "title": "Pilot Officer Edward Platt 137558, Navigator, 78 Squadron",
      "publisher": "CWGC",
      "tier": "official",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-28",
      "summary": "CWGC story about Platt. Cites the accident record card: the aircraft were diverted from Breighton, Leconfield could not take them, and they collided on the way to Hutton Cranswick. Lists the BB373 crew.",
      "key_details": [
        "Platt on IBCC Panel 226",
        "family memorial at Bury Cemetery, Redvales"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S4",
